<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif">Agent</span></span><br>
&nbsp;</p>

<hr>
<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif"><strong>Non Waiver</strong>:&nbsp;If you make a payment of&nbsp;less than the&nbsp;<u><strong><span contenteditable="false">[[Rent_Balance]]</span></strong></u>&nbsp;required by this notice, you will still be in default and&nbsp;SUBJECT TO EVICTION&nbsp;unless the Owner agrees in writing to cancel this notice.</span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif"><strong>Credit reporting</strong>:&nbsp;We may report delinquent accounts to credit bureaus. This may affect your ability to obtain credit and or your ability to rent in the future</span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif"><strong>Double Rent</strong>:&nbsp;Wisconsin law §704.27 provides that an owner can recover a&nbsp;minimum of twice the daily rent&nbsp;amount for the time the tenant remains in possession of the unit after expiration of this notice.</span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif">Skipping out&nbsp;is against the law in Wisconsin. Statute 943.215: "Absconding without paying rent. (1) Whoever having obtained the tenancy, as defined in s. 704.01 (4) of residential property he or she is entitled to occupy, intentionally absconds without paying all current and past due rent is guilty of a Class A misdemeanor."</span></span></p>

<hr>
<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif">Arrangement for payment can be made through your <a href="https://yawdcour.managebuilding.com/Resident/public/home" target="_blank">Tenant Portal</a></span></span></p>', array['Current_Month', 'Current_Year', 'Lease_All_Tenants', 'Lease_Rent_Due_Day', 'Rent_Balance', 'Rental_Owner_Full_Name', 'Unit_Address_Line_1', 'Unit_City_Address', 'Unit_Number', 'Unit_PostalCode_Address', 'Unit_State_Address']::text[]) on conflict (buildium_id) do update set html = excluded.html, fields = excluded.fields, subject = excluded.subject, description = excluded.description;
