<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif"><span contenteditable="false">[[Unit_City_Address]]</span>, <span contenteditable="false">[[Unit_State_Address]]</span> <span contenteditable="false">[[Unit_PostalCode_Address]]</span></span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif">This notice terminates your tenancy pursuant to §704.17 (1) or (2)(b), Wisconsin Statutes, and requires you to remedy the breach described below OR vacate the premises described in this notice within 5 days from service hereof.</span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif">Description of premises: <span contenteditable="false">[[Unit_Address_Line_1]]</span>, <span contenteditable="false">[[Unit_Number]]</span>, Milwaukee WI <span contenteditable="false">[[Unit_PostalCode_Address]]</span>.</span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif">You have breached the terms of your Rental Agreement as follows:</span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif">You are in violation of Rule #52 of the Rules and Regulations incorporated into your Lease Agreement, which states:</span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif">"<em>Pets are not permitted on the property at any time without the prior written consent of Landlord.</em>"</span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif">To remedy this breach and avoid eviction, you must take the following action:</span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif">You must immediately remove all unauthorized pets from the premises and correct any sanitary issues caused by said pets.</span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif"><strong>Liability for Damages</strong>: <em>Please take notice that under the terms of your lease and Wisconsin law, you are financially responsible for any property damage caused by unauthorized animals. This includes, but is not limited to, costs for professional cleaning, deodorizing, carpet replacement, subfloor treatment, and drywall repair necessary to restore the premises to its original condition</em>.</span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif">If you fail to comply with this demand to remedy the breach within five (5) days, your tenancy will be terminated, and you will be required to surrender possession of the premises.</span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif">Dated at Milwaukee, WI 53224, this _______ day of <span contenteditable="false">[[Current_Month]]</span> <span contenteditable="false">[[Current_Year]]</span></span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif">Landlord / Landlord''s Agent:</span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif"><span contenteditable="false">[[Rental_Owner_Full_Name]]</span> / Albert Harris</span></span></p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif">Agent</span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif">Non Waiver: Acceptance of rent or any other partial performance by the Tenant after the service of this notice does not constitute a waiver of the Landlord''s right to terminate the tenancy for the breach described above, unless the Landlord agrees in writing to cancel this notice.</span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif">Double Rent: Wisconsin law §704.27 provides that an owner can recover a minimum of twice the daily rent amount for the time the tenant remains in possession of the unit after expiration of this notice.</span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size: 1.5em"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif">Skipping out is against the law in Wisconsin. Statute 943.215: "Absconding without paying rent. (1) Whoever having obtained the tenancy, as defined in s. 704.01 (4) of residential property he or she is entitled to occupy, intentionally absconds without paying all current and past due rent is guilty of a Class A misdemeanor."</span></span></p>', array['Current_Month', 'Current_Year', 'Lease_All_Tenants', 'Rental_Owner_Full_Name', 'Unit_Address_Line_1', 'Unit_City_Address', 'Unit_Number', 'Unit_PostalCode_Address', 'Unit_State_Address']::text[]) on conflict (buildium_id) do update set html = excluded.html, fields = excluded.fields, subject = excluded.subject, description = excluded.description;
